In the LEAF Help Library HTML file, replace the .hl-hero CSS rule block and the .hl-hero HTML markup with the versions below. This changes the hero from a flat navy block to a diagonal gradient with faint decorative corner icons, a personalized greeting, and an updated subtitle. Icon set uses the same material-symbols-outlined font already loaded elsewhere in the file (menu_book, smart_display, help, lightbulb) so no new icon dependency is introduced. The greeting name should come from whatever variable/session data already provides the logged-in user's first name elsewhere in the app (e.g. wherever "Welcome, Stephanie Lumagui" is rendered in the nav) — swap the placeholder accordingly.

CSS — replace the existing .hl-hero rule:

css
.hl-hero {
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
  background: linear-gradient(120deg, #1e4d7a 0%, #2570b5 65%, #3d8fc9 100%);
  padding: 48px 24px;
  text-align: center;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hl-border-soft);
}
.hl-hero::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background-image:
    radial-gradient(ellipse 200px 120px at 10% 20%, rgba(255,255,255,0.06) 0%, transparent 70%),
    radial-gradient(ellipse 300px 200px at 85% 80%, rgba(255,255,255,0.05) 0%, transparent 70%);
  pointer-events: none;
}
.hl-hero-deco {
  position: absolute;
  font-size: 42px;
  color: #fff;
  opacity: 0.13;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.hl-hero-deco--book   { top: 16px; left: 26px; transform: rotate(-12deg); }
.hl-hero-deco--video  { bottom: 14px; left: 84px; transform: rotate(8deg); }
.hl-hero-deco--help   { top: 20px; right: 74px; transform: rotate(10deg); }
.hl-hero-deco--bulb   { bottom: 16px; right: 26px; transform: rotate(-8deg); }

.hl-hero-inner {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 1;
}
.hl-hero-greeting {
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);
  margin: 0 0 2px;
}
.hl-hero h1 {
  font-family: "Public Sans", sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.75rem;
  font-weight: 800;
  color: #fff;
  margin: 0 0 6px;
}
.hl-hero p.hl-hero-sub {
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
  margin: 0 0 22px;
}

HTML — replace the existing hero block:

html
<div class="hl-hero">
  <span class="material-symbols-outlined hl-hero-deco hl-hero-deco--book" aria-hidden="true">menu_book</span>
  <span class="material-symbols-outlined hl-hero-deco hl-hero-deco--video" aria-hidden="true">smart_display</span>
  <span class="material-symbols-outlined hl-hero-deco hl-hero-deco--help" aria-hidden="true">help</span>
  <span class="material-symbols-outlined hl-hero-deco hl-hero-deco--bulb" aria-hidden="true">lightbulb</span>

  <div class="hl-hero-inner">
    <p class="hl-hero-greeting">Hello, {{firstName}}.</p>
    <h1>What are we solving today?</h1>
    <p class="hl-hero-sub">Tutorials, videos, and guides, all in one place.</p>
    <div class="hl-sbox" role="search">
      <label for="sq" class="hl-sr-only">Search help library</label>
      <input
        id="sq"
        type="search"
        placeholder='Try "report", "user access"…'
        autocomplete="off"
      />
      <button
        class="hl-sbox-btn"
        id="sqBtn"
        type="button"
        tabindex="0"
        aria-label="Submit search"
      >
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">search</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

Notes for the agent:

{{firstName}} needs to be swapped for the actual server-side/JS variable holding the logged-in user's first name — check how "Welcome, Stephanie Lumagui" is populated in the nav bar and reuse that same source, parsed to first name only.
If no name is available (e.g. session not loaded yet, or anonymous access), fall back to just "Hello." with no name, or omit the greeting line entirely — don't render "Hello, undefined."
menu_book, smart_display, help, and lightbulb are new icon names not currently in your icon list — add them to whatever inventory/download list you're building for self-hosting the icon font.
The existing .hl-sbox search box markup and styles are unchanged — just moved inside .hl-hero-inner.
